ed to run off rogue or just died  two turrets we change service  immediately we can some rogues  but then again due to the communication  issues we were split in two while I was  frantically trying to keep up with Marco  we came across a group of four rogues  trying to extract as we had the jump on  them even with just the two of us on  controllers we were able to quickly drop  the entire squad before they knew what  was going on I was a little too excited  to really embrace the new cover shooter  mechanics but because they had no idea  of what was going on at didn't matter  the next group found us for v2 without  the element of surprise we will quickly  take him down this played out a few more  times and although I'd say staying  behind cover isn't the only way it  certainly gave out a bit of an advantage  no matter what we tried cover was a much  better way to take on a face-to-face  battle  next we were down to try out some  conflict domination as you'd expect this  new PvP mode puts two teams of four  against each other the objective is to  capture the zones and hold them to gain  points I'll be the first to admit I  spent a lot of this time trying out new  weapons and exploring the random site  objectives around the map one of which  seem to give a mode which is  specialization my usual tactics of  running out and holding my own wasn't  working it felt like there was a lot  more teamwork involved again it was hard  to break the habit of the usual chicken  dance style of PvP but a couple of  players utilizing cover mechanics  properly would quickly shut you down  unless you hit the bus pros I won't go  into the details of the healing and  weapons of the stage as I'll be covering  them in more depth in the next video but  the majority of what I know about PvP  has changed and as much as I like PvP in  the division I completely agree that was  a bit weird and I welcome this change we  will meet to try out some conflicts  skirmish two but due to running out of  time we must up summing up there are a  number of changes coming to the dark  zone focusing on reducing the toxicity  and the player skill gap with the  intention of having more people getting  involved but with the introduction of  the darker zone we may be seeing the DZ  that we had in the beginning of division  1 making your turn PvP still has a  similar feel to what we currently have  but with more emphasis on the cover  shooter mechanics the division was  always intended to be based around long  story short the feelings I had playing  these game modes don't change the game  for me what we're all used to is still  there  but now we have to mix up the PvP style  of play solely relying on the chicken  dance just doesn't cut it anymore we  weren't able to play the game for long  enough to really break down what the new  meta style of play will be but at this  stage it does have a feel of being more  strategic and team orientated otherwise  I'll see you in the next video we will  dive a little deeper into some of the  skills and other game mechanics that  we're able to have a play with Cheers  [Music]  you

